# ScriptLens Architecture

## Source of Truth

- `docs/source/task.md` — highest-priority requirement source, never modified.
- `docs/01-requirements.md` — product requirements, Agent output schema, 5 scoring dimensions, acceptance checklist.
- `docs/00-reuse-matrix.md` — ScholarMind → ScriptLens module reuse matrix and 3-day execution plan.

Any work that does not serve `task.md` is out of scope.

## Backend Layout (single-service architecture)

ScriptLens runs as **one FastAPI process** (`scriptlens_api:8005`). The ReAct Agent is embedded as a subpackage inside `app/`, not a separate microservice. See `00-reuse-matrix.md §0.1` for rationale.

| Path | Source | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `backend/app/` | physically copied from `ScholarMind/backend/app/` per `00-reuse-matrix.md §2-§3` | main API: users, script library, documents, jobs, sessions, simplified RAG, 5-dimension report pipeline |
| `backend/app/agent_runtime/` | physically copied from `ScholarMind/backend/services/doc_studio/` per `00-reuse-matrix.md §4` and migrated per §0.1 | ReAct subpackage: agent_service, async_run_manager, HitL, tool registry, script-specific tools |

## Backend Boundaries

- `app/router/` exposes HTTP; thin layer, no business logic.
- `app/service/core/ingestion/` parses uploads (docx / pdf / txt / md, no legacy .doc) and segments by `第N集` / `X-Y 场号` / `角色：对白` / `角色 os：内心` anchors.
- `app/service/script_rag.py` runs simplified RAG: embedding + BM25 → RRF → top-k. No HyDE, no metadata boost, no cross-encoder rerank.
- `app/service/script_report_service.py` orchestrates the deterministic 5-dimension scoring pipeline (D2-4). It does NOT use the ReAct loop; ReAct is reserved for chat / rewrite where multi-step reasoning is genuinely needed.
- `app/agent_runtime/service/agent_service.py` runs the ReAct loop. Called in-process from chat / rewrite endpoints; never via HTTP.
- `app/agent_runtime/service/tools/` contains the Agent tool registry: 4 script-specific tools (`score_dimension_tool`, `locate_scenes_tool`, `extract_characters_tool`, `propose_rewrite_tool`) plus reused tools (`web_search_tool`, `analysis_tools`, editing tools). All inherit `BaseTool` for budget guarding and consecutive-failure recovery.
- `app/agent_runtime/` uses **relative imports only** (`from .core.config`, `from .service.X`). Its `core/config.py` is independent from `app/core/config.py`; pydantic_settings reads the same `.env` but field names do not collide.
- DO NOT add an independent FastAPI process for the Agent. If a future scaling need genuinely demands it, lift `app/agent_runtime/` out as a sibling `services/scriptlens_agent/` package — the subpackage boundary is designed to make this trivial.

## Out of Scope (DO NOT BUILD)

- DeepResearch, Notebook, IdeaGen, Admin console.
- Online ingestion (Semantic Scholar, arXiv).
- LaTeX compile, ctex, bibtex.
- Cross-session long-term memory.
- Reranker container, MinerU, Grobid, Elasticsearch.
- Per-user workspace isolation beyond `users` row.
- 6-role full perspective system; only 3 roles in MVP: selection / writer / review.
- Independent Agent microservice (subpackage in-process only — see Backend Layout above).
- RL training, reward model, full skill scheduler (only the lightweight feedback-injection skill mechanism in PRD §10 P3).

## Agent Output Rules

- Every score / claim must carry non-empty `evidence_ref_ids[]`.
- Empty-evidence outputs are treated as LLM hallucination and dropped before being shown to the user.
- Structured JSON over prose for any output consumed by code (see schema in `docs/01-requirements.md §7`).
- Fail loudly on schema mismatch or missing source file; never silently fall back.

## Frontend Layout

| Path | Source | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `frontend/src/pages/script-studio/` | physically copied from `ScholarMind/frontend/src/pages/doc-studio/` per `00-reuse-matrix.md §7` | left script viewer (txt + scene tree + evidence highlight) + right Agent chat + report tab |
| `frontend/src/pages/script-library/` | physically copied from `ScholarMind/frontend/src/pages/repository/` | upload + list + delete; no online import |

## Frontend Contract Rules

- TypeScript types mirror backend Pydantic schemas exactly.
- Click-through from claim → `evidence_ref_id` → highlight in left source viewer is mandatory.
- Do not hide backend errors behind generic success states.

## Deployment

Reuse existing `portfolio-mvp-shanghai-01` ECS. New container `scriptlens_api` only. Shared PostgreSQL (independent schema `scriptlens`), shared Redis (`REDIS_DB=1`), shared Cloudflare Tunnel (new hostname `api-scriptlens.wh5233.me`).
